WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.702
-Please, welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.303
"The Tonight Show," everybody!

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:07.640
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.541
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:11.577
Well, guys, today the CDC

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.013
made a huge announcement
about wearing masks.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.215
Watch this.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.583
-The CDC now says that
vaccinated Americans

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.252
generally do not need
to wear masks outside

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:23.022
as long as they're
not in a large gathering.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.957
-When people heard that,
people in the street started

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.726
flashing their mouths
like it was Mardi Gras.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.029
Like, whoo!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:34.033
Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.369
I got to be honest, I'm gonna
miss wearing a mask.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.338
The adult acne
made me feel young.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.907
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.808
On the bright side,
now we can finally stop

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.978
weirdly opening our eyes
to greet people on the street.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:49.048
Like --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.718
That's right.
The CDC updated its guidance on

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.686
outdoor masking
for both vaccinated

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.555
and unvaccinated people.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.223
And they even released
this helpful chart.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.657
Take a look at this.

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.027
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, I like to think

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:03.162
the sketch artist
at the CDC is like,

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:07.233
"I'll tell you, I can do hair,
ears, eyes, and mouth.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.269
I just don't do noses."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:13.906
I just don't --
It's just not my thing."

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:17.777
The two most important things
about a -- Ah.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.211
"I'll do it for cheap,
I'll do it for cheap.

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:21.647
I just don't do them."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.215
The chart ranks activities

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:26.385
from safest to less safe
to least safe.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.854
It's the same chart people use
when deciding between

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.456
Delta, United,
and Spirit Airlines.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.259
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.428
Well, it's a big week
for President Biden.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.731 line:0%
Tomorrow he delivers his first
joint address to Congress.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.467
Yep, everyone is looking forward
to hearing Biden speak.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.601
Then, at the last minute,

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.737
they're going to call on
Anthony Hopkins instead.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.339
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.339 --> 00:01:49.642
It's always interesting to watch
a presidential address.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.711
Half the crowd cheers,
half the crowd sits in silence.

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:54.813
It's like a throwback
to Harry and Meghan's wedding,

00:01:54.813 --> 00:02:01.254
don't you think?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.857
Yeah, Biden's address will be
on all of the major networks.

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.927
Of course, on Telemundo, Biden
will be dubbed in Spanish,

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.963
and on Fox News,
he'll be dubbed by a demon.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:13.433
-[ Speaking demonic ]

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:18.404
[ Applause ]

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.073
-Some tech news --
After a long wait,

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:24.610
Apple rolled out a new privacy
feature that requires apps

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.580
like Facebook to ask permission
before tracking

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.582
the activity on your iPhone.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:35.021
Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:38.491
So now you can relax at home
in total privacy.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.426
-Yes, total privacy.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.861
Ha-ha-ha.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.731
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:48.334
-Yeah, after years of infringing
on our privacy, Apple is like,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.204
"We're against collecting
your data, starting now."

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.571
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.574
Apple also introduced
new emojis,

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:59.379
including face exhaling
and face in clouds.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.513
Take a look.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:05.218
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.985
Even the eggplant emoji is like,

00:03:06.985 --> 00:03:08.854
"Come on, we all know what this
is supposed to be."

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.156
[ Laughter ]
-Come on.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.892
-"We gonna play this game?
We gonna play this game?"

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.395
[ Cheers and applause ]
Okay. Come on.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.998
I saw that Guinness
just debuted a new beer

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.434
with Nitro Cold Brew Coffee
in it.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.135
Check it out.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.639
Yeah. It's the perfect gift for
the sluggish drunk in your life.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.541
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.044
It's a great product if you want
your heart to feel like it's

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.912
napping and skydiving
at the same time.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.114
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.417
It should be fun walking around
the office with a can of that.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.619
Like, [Slurred] "9:00 a.m.,
time for another pick-me-up."

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.955
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.158
[ Normal voice ] That's right,
Guinness and coffee.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.160
Irish people call that
baby formula.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.428
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.865
And another unlikely pairing --
Goldfish has teamed up

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:56.435
with Frank's RedHot for new
limited-edition spicy crackers.

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:57.803
Here's a photo.

00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:59.405
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.975
And normally I make a joke about
these kind of food mash-ups,

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.142
but I'm going to level with you.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.677
This one sounds spectacular.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.078
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.279
Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.782
Right? When it comes to
recent innovations,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.819
I put the COVID vaccine at 1,
this at 1A.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.221
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.355
To some it sounds weird,

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.357
but it's still better than
Gerber Sriracha.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:23.396
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.565
Welcome back -- Baby hot ones!

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:29.368
[ Laughter ]
-Come on.

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:32.004
-Hey, some good news
for Dunkin' Donuts fans.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:33.205
They just announced
they're adding

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.474
coconut milk to the menu.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.410
Yep, they'll keep it
on the table

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.245
between the cream
and the ashtray.

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.714
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:42.815
And if you order it, legally

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.483
they're allowed
to make fun of you.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:47.820
"I got a large iced coffee
for Prince Brandon,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.155
who's too good for cows.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.925
That's Brandon,
B as in bee-atch!"

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:57.263
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:59.298
And finally some news
from overseas.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.701
I read that next month
a high-end apartment complex

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.270
in London is opening up
a see-through pool

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.372
that sits 115 feet high.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.340
Look at this thing.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.209
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.778
-It's perfect 'cause when I
think sunny rooftop pools,

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.280
I think London.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.517
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:21.420
You know someone's last words
are gonna be, "Cannonball!"

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.389
Hey, Quest, welcome back
and congratulations, buddy.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.557
-Hey, thank you.
-That was fantastic.

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.460
Questlove.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.963
The musical director
for the Academy Awards!

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.865
-Yes.
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.067
-Dude, you looked great.
You sounded great.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.802
What was it like?

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.337
Were you -- Was it weird?

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:39.872
Were you nervous?
-It was fun.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:43.643
I mean, that's the first time
that I have been out anywhere

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.078
since the last Oscars, so...

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.313
-Wow.
-You know.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.148
But, no, it was fun.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.050
It was a little party, you know.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.051
-Yeah.
-We had fun.

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:56.288
-But that opening where
Regina grabbed the Oscar,

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:57.523
you were doing that?

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.858
-Oh, man, that was so hard.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.893
We had to perfectly time --
-Right?

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.696
I was sweating for you, dude.
I was like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.631
-Yeah, I didn't think
she was gonna make it.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:06.999
But I kept extending it

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:09.769
and looking at the end marking,
yeah.

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:11.971
-And then the biggest moment
of the night,

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:15.408
besides Daniel Kaluuya,
was Glenn Close.

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.509
-Yeah.
-Doing "Da Butt."

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:19.445
-Who knew that she knew
"Da Butt"?

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.946
[ Laughter ]
-No, I did not know.

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:21.947
But she's fun.

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.916
-Everyone asked,
"Was that scripted?"

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.384
Really, we didn't prepare her.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:28.854
She just -- We told her
something was gonna happen,

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.522
but she didn't know.
-Yeah, you never know what

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.892
someone's gonna do.
Of course, she so is game.

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:34.493
-Yeah.
-She's so much fun.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.629
Remember when she came on
the show and we had a contest,

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.564
how many baby carrots
can we fit in our mouths?

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.898
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.898 --> 00:06:42.568
It's like, "What is going on?"
She was just so game.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.702
She was like,
"Let's do it, why not?"

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:44.971
-That's how I knew
she was game for this.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.739
-Yeah, I love --
Anyways, it was great, buddy.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.040
Congratulations.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.778
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:54.112
-This is big.

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:57.216
The Census Bureau just released
their findings for 2020.

00:06:57.216 --> 00:07:00.285
And according to the data,
there are --

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:01.887
these are some
fun facts for you --

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:05.191
331 million people living in
the United States.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.526
-Ooh.
-Pretty interesting.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:10.563
In fact, there were a lot of
surprising results

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.264
from the Census here.
-Really?

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:13.533
-Yeah. Check out some of these.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:18.704 line:0%
First up, 489,000 people
are named Jeff,

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:22.007 line:0%
but for reasons no one can
explain, spelled G-E-O-F-F.

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:22.941 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:22.941 --> 00:07:24.209
-Wow.
-Geoff.

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:25.778
-Geoff.
-Yeah.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:27.946
-489,000, that's a lot.

00:07:27.946 --> 00:07:31.750 line:0%
-Look at this -- 11 million
people think the Quaker Oats guy

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.185 line:0%
is a Founding Father.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:33.185 --> 00:07:35.321
-11?

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:37.723
-I might be one of them.
-Yeah.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:42.328
-Check out this next result --
7.5 million people don't know

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.563
if reindeer are real
and are afraid to ask.

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:47.800
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.669
-But they answered
the census though.

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:52.004
-Yeah, of course.
Yeah, of course.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.972
Yeah, they're afraid to ask.
-That's a specific question.

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:55.408
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:58.444 line:0%
Look at this -- 3.5 million
people believe Mount Rushmore

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:59.778 line:0%
is a natural rock formation

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:01.447 line:0%
that just happens
to look like four presidents.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:02.848
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's insane.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:05.685
-Crazy.
-That's impossible.

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:07.486
-More than Geoff.
-Yeah.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.188
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:12.491
Up next, 20 million people
can't describe a goatee

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:13.759
without using their hands.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:17.529
[ Laughter ]
"It's like a --

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:18.698
That."
-Yeah.

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:19.998
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:21.367
-How about this one here?

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:24.003
750,000 people think Elon Musk

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.470
is a cologne
they sell at Walgreens.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.572
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.106
I remember wearing it
in high school.

00:08:28.106 --> 00:08:31.076
-That was Drakkar Noir.
-Yeah.

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:36.082
-And finally, 165 million people
"literally can't even" anymore.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:38.017
I literally can't even.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:39.385
I learned a lot. Stick around.

